{"name":"Memorial Black","hex":"#091101","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"memorial","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Memory; recollection. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Something, such as a monument, by which someone or something is remembered."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Serving as a remembrance of someone or something; commemorative.","Contained in the memory."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/memorial"},{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"}],"entries":[{"title":"Memorial","blocks":[{"text":"A memorial is an object or place which serves as a focus for the memory or the commemoration of something, usually an influential, deceased person or a historical, tragic event. Popular forms of memorials include landmark objects such as homes or other sites, or works of art such as sculptures, statues, fountains or parks. Larger memorials may be known as monuments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/JHAVARD.MONMASON.MaryCarpenter.Wall-mounted_memorial.BristolCath.jpg/330px-JHAVARD.MONMASON.MaryCarpenter.Wall-mounted_memorial.BristolCath.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memorial","wikidata":"Q5003624"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Louisa_lawson_suffragette_light_box_memorial_greenway.JPG/500px-Louisa_lawson_suffragette_light_box_memorial_greenway.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Louisa_lawson_suffragette_light_box_memorial_greenway.JPG/1280px-Louisa_lawson_suffragette_light_box_memorial_greenway.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Louisa_lawson_suffragette_light_box_memorial_greenway.JPG/500px-Louisa_lawson_suffragette_light_box_memorial_greenway.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lightbox used as a memorial.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALouisa_lawson_suffragette_light_box_memorial_greenway.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Haymarket-martyrs-memorial-Forest-Home-Cemetery-IL.jpg/250px-Haymarket-martyrs-memorial-Forest-Home-Cemetery-IL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Haymarket-martyrs-memorial-Forest-Home-Cemetery-IL.jpg/250px-Haymarket-martyrs-memorial-Forest-Home-Cemetery-IL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHaymarket-martyrs-memor